    "reasoning": "Rule ACC-006 rejects orders with HER2 evaluation (Breast IHC Panel includes HER2) when fixation_time_hours is outside the [6.0, 72.0]h clinical tolerance. Three orders violate this requirement and were transitioned to DO_NOT_PROCESS: ORD-2301 (96.0h, over the 72h ceiling), ORD-2303 (84.0h, over the 72h ceiling), and ORD-2310 (4.0h, under the 6h floor). ORD-2304 (12.0h) and ORD-2305 (18.0h) have Breast IHC Panel ordered but fixation is within tolerance. ORD-2311 is in DO_NOT_PROCESS but its fixation (30.0h) is within tolerance and its flag (INADEQUATE_SAMPLE_REJECTION) names the actual rejection reason — it is not a HER2 fixation failure. Orders with only H&E (ORD-2302, ORD-2306, ORD-2309) are not subject to ACC-006. ORD-2307 and ORD-2308 are past the ACCESSIONING gate where ACC-006 applies; their null fixation reflects post-accessioning data shedding, not an active fixation check."
